{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557308-jam-weapon-query","id":1557308,"title":"Jam Weapon Query","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-05T08:11:13-08:00","id":1557308,"title":"Jam Weapon Query","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> Me and the boys were having a little discussion on how Jam Weapon (R1 CoG Gift, W20 Core pg.177) works. And we think your inputs would weigh in here and help us understand the exact purpose of this Gift. We looked at it from 2 angles: 1) taking into consideration of the Tribe, 2) how its a rank 1 gift and actual physics.<br /> <br /> The following are our conclusions and we'd like to hear from the chads of Gaia on this<br /> <br /> 1- Tribe angle: CoG are the kind of Garou who'd fit such a gift, also taught by cool guy 'Dove' to neutralize all weapons possible - be it guns, knives, blunt, etc. as long as they've had the touch of Weaver involved. As the book specifies that blades don't cut and rocks can hurt.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Mystical Gift that is rolled against Willpower disables ALL weapons for its effect range, as it is about peace from Weaver by any means.<br /> <br /> 2- Rank 1 + physics angle: Rank 1 Gifts are useful in many ways and some Gifts are quite strong at the rank 1 level itself. Could this just be one of those niche strong gifts or we draw the line with physics that force and strength still account here.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Just an extremely useful Gift with no question on whether guns would work. But someone can pistol whip and deal damage. Similarly, lethal damage (such as blades) turn to bashing but apply the same damage. Or maybe even lose the 'STR+value' bonus and roll the strength alone.<br /> <br /> Sidebar:<br /> How would silver weapons work here? a) an ore of silver being thrown b) silver sword c) silver klaive<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12544-diplo","name":"diplo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12544_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T11:06:14-08:00","id":1557313,"title":"","content":"With WTA, gifts work because they are spiritual power, the pact you have with the spirit world, grants you the right to do what the Gift states. You spend Gnosis, or Willpower, or whatever is required; roll the relevant stats (if any), and then the magic happens.<br /> <br /> Trying to use physics makes no sense in the game as shown, because of &quot;spirit magic reasons&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, yes, the gift is powerful, and it is open to interpretation: if the knife does not cut, can I still kill someone by jamming their throat or airways with it? Can I just move fast and hard enough as a blunt object?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-21-2026, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T11:27:37-08:00","id":1557314,"title":"","content":"I think the description of the Gift is fairly clear.<br /> <br /> All manufactured weapons (within range of the Garou's voice) will not function for one turn per success.<br /> <br /> Natural weapons and natural objects appropriated as weapons are unaffected.<br /> <br /> So what happens if you use a weapon not as intended, using it to pistol whip as in your post. Well, we know a Garou could use a rock or naturally fallen tree limb (presumably to get that extra die of damage or whatever the ST assigns to it). So can you use a pistol the same way?<br /> <br /> I would argue &quot;no&quot;. The fact the description says &quot;naturally fallen&quot; tree limb, and not just tree limb indicates any purposeful fashioning of natural materials are negated by the gift. A tree limb that has fallen onto the ground isn't negated. An identical tree limb that is purposefully removed to be used as a tool/weapon is negated. The act of human/Garou (even tool using animals IMO) manipulation/creation means the Gift works against it.<br /> <br /> That also includes things that normally aren't considered weapons, but could be used as such. That chair or glass bottle will continue to work as chair or glass bottle for its normal purposes, but if someone intends to use them as weapons, they can't harm people.<br /> <br /> Sam logic applies to anything silver.<br /> <br /> Most silver ores probably count as rocks and could be used. However, I would be willing to consider whether ore that is mined by human hands qualifies it as an &quot;unnatural&quot; object. I think different people will come to different conclusions on this. As such, I would defer to the consensus at my local gaming table.<br /> <br /> Silver swords and silver klaives are clearly manufactured weapons, and they don't work in terms of providing extra dice. However, they are STILL silver. So does merely touching such silver cause the one level of aggravated damage per turn of contact (unless in breed form)? I would say YES because the silver damage does not occur because silver is a weapon, but because it is just silver. (In my chronicles, I say that the Garou vulnerability to silver is a result of the pact with Luna that gave them their shapeshifting. It's old chiminage. Garou can shapeshift by the blessing of Luna in exchange for their vulnerability to the lunar metal, silver.) That doesn't go away simply because an object is a weapon.<br /> <br /> However, that also means such a silver weapon ONLY does one level of aggravated damage per &quot;touch&quot;. You can't do multiple levels of damage like a weapon would normally do (like the Strength +2 of a klaive). Nor any other abilities such silver weapons/fetishes might do.<br /> <br /> Likewise the presence of silver should be affecting Gnosis as appropriate. Might not mean anything to the defender, but it would apply to the attacker wielding silver weapons.<br /> <br /> This would be my initial ruling, but would be willing to consider other opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T03:40:59-08:00","id":1557341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>diplo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557308-jam-weapon-query#post1557308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we'd like to hear from the chads of Gaia on this</div> </div> </div> </div>What the fuck?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T06:11:57-08:00","id":1557376,"title":"","content":"Important lesson about WTA powers, IMO, is that level 1 powers aren't weakened by being level 1 powers. Sure, if a spirit is &quot;immune to any Gift below level 5&quot;, or if a Gift allows you to override Level 1 and 2 Gifts, there's that. But generally speaking, a level 1 Gift does EXACTLY what it says it does, even if that's absurdly strong.<br /> <br /> Spirit Speech is far more powerful than many high-level Gifts. Mother's Touch is an insane healing ability which almost every healing group in the WoD would envy, before you even consider that it's available at char-gen.<br /> <br /> With that in mind...<br /> <br /> Yes, Jam Weapon CAN stop a nuke from going off. It can stop missiles, it can stop the legendary blade of an ancient fae king, it can stop all of the plasma cannons attached to the HIT Mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T12:06:29-08:00","id":1557377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557308-jam-weapon-query?p=1557314#post1557314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be my initial ruling, but would be willing to consider other opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically the ruling the books leave us with.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> Though I would say IME the Gift is also just kinda... unfun. It's both extremely powerful and completely worthless depending on the situation. The range of &quot;voice&quot; could be feet or miles depending on circumstance, but the bigger the range the more likely a high WP target is around to reduce the effectiveness of the Gift. It's also completely unclear if understanding the voice or hearing the voice clearly matters. Since it's indiscriminant, you don't want to use it if any of your allies use weapons as their primary combat mode unless everyone agrees it's better to go unarmed. The duration is also fairly short so you can't take advantage of that range unless you have some high end Gifts that can attack at a similar distance (which do exist) or it's part of a fairly large coordinated effort.<br /> <br /> I also feel like despite it being flavored to match the Children of Gaia in theme... it's way better as a Red Talon Gift. If you think about olden days where Garou would more actively fight over Caerns, Jam Weapon would easily be the go-to opening move of any Red Talon Sept on offense or defense. Homid kinfolk are battlefield liabilities as long as this Gift is maintained, while wolf-kin are unaffected. Most of the other Tribes have their favored weapons that means at least some of their fighting force would be reduced without access to swords, hammers, axes, or bows; even if only for a few turns. Red Talons being all Crinos or Wolf born also means more default Gnosis so they can have backline Cliaths keep up the effect from a distance while experienced fighters press the advantage.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say even as a Gift that might exist more as flavor than practical use (which I don't like, but it's part of the game as written), it feels like it's in the wrong place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}